{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman","id":905932,"title":"wolverine post Hugh Jackman","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-02T14:06:30-07:00","id":905932,"title":"wolverine post Hugh Jackman","content":"Since there is the possibility of at least 1 maybe even 2 more Xmen films with the current cast line up, including wolvie popping in at least one of those, and since Hugh has said he is done playing Logan.. Who do you think would be a good fit to take over the role??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:30:18-07:00","id":906005,"title":"","content":"I say dont do a recasting like with the others. Instead, turn the franchise over to X-23<br /> <br /> Now, who should play her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:37:12-07:00","id":906250,"title":"","content":"Someone mentioned that elsewhere, but<br /> A) X-23 is something only recently done for comics, so i doubt the franchise of films would be close to that level timeline wise<br /> B) not everyone watching has read any of the comics, so just switching it up like that could seriously throw some fans of the films off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T00:11:35-07:00","id":906263,"title":"","content":"If not X-23, there's always Daken. He's a lot easier to introduce since he's Logan's biological son, and is aware of this fact. Half-Japanese Half-Caucasian also opens up a lot of casting options since you aren't trying to find someone to replace Jackman directly. If you've watched the X-Men movies, it's been established that Logan was in Japan during WWII, so the idea of him having a kid there, and who's whatever age the actor is because Daken share's in the extremely slow aging benefit of their healing factor, is really easy to write into the story:<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be hard to have whatever removes Logan from the story drag Daken into the lime-light, and the switch would be less abrupt for those that don't read the comics since, again, it's his son from a period that fits the movie chronology (however mangled it is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:18:19-07:00","id":906663,"title":"","content":"No way is Daken in the picture. X-23 is a sure bet as a recent casting choice squares almost perfectly with Laura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:54:20-07:00","id":906687,"title":"","content":"Never knew logan had a kid.. Was it with Mariko?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:38:03-07:00","id":906796,"title":"","content":"Besides not liking Daken... is there any reason he couldn't be a replacement for Logan if they don't want to recast him after Jackman leaves?<br /> <br /> Also, who's this recent casting that's a ringer for Laura? I haven't seen anything for new X-Men franchise castings since the new movie, and all the ones that might be here have other parts.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> <br /> And Daken's birth mother was named Itsu.. and she doesn't really show up much besides her fling with Logan, getting pregnant, and dying (before giving birth... but those Wolverines are tough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:03:56-07:00","id":906934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=906796#post906796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides not liking Daken... is there any reason he couldn't be a replacement for Logan if they don't want to recast him after Jackman leaves?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO its more that most people don't even know who he is if you mention him..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T23:34:07-07:00","id":907002,"title":"","content":"So are all of the other characters that have replaced Logan as Wolverine for any period of time (save Mystique... but well... that's not exactly going to work).<br /> <br /> The MCU and Deadpool both showed that lesser known characters in the Marvel canon can work on the screen just fine. Most people don't know who 90% of the main Marvel canon characters are. Any replacement/legacy character needs to be introduced in the movies, which is a hurdle simply recasting Logan doesn't suffer, but also doesn't run into the issue of, &quot;why doesn't Logan look the same anymore?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:15:46-07:00","id":907010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907002#post907002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are all of the other characters that have replaced Logan as Wolverine for any period of time (save Mystique... but well... that's not exactly going to work).<br /> <br /> The MCU and <b>Deadpool both showed that lesser known characters in the Marvel</b> canon can work on the screen just fine. Most people don't know who 90% of the main Marvel canon characters are. Any replacement/legacy character needs to be introduced in the movies, which is a hurdle simply recasting Logan doesn't suffer, but also doesn't run into the issue of, &quot;why doesn't Logan look the same anymore?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Deadpool was/is not a lesser known character. Deadpool has been one of the most well known characters in comics since his debut. It was the lack of faith in Fox that made his movie success so insanely out of the ordinary. <br /> <br /> A better example would've been Guardians of the Galaxy. <br /> <br /> Daken is a crap character that is no longer used. <b>X-23 is a popular character is is currently the star of her very own comic.</b> That is the difference. And it's a big one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T02:21:27-07:00","id":907037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907010#post907010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deadpool was/is not a lesser known character.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.... but everyone else in the movie besides Colossus is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A better example would've been Guardians of the Galaxy. </div> </div> </div>That would be under the header of the general MCU (since there are more examples than just the Guardians in there).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Daken is a crap character that is no longer used. </div> </div> </div>He hasn't been used... in a year. It's Marvel. That means jack-shit to whether or not they'll bring him back (esp. with Laura's book, it seems inevitable that he'll at least get a recurring role down the line there).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>X-23 is a popular character is is currently the star of her very own comic.</b> That is the difference. And it's a big one. </div> </div> </div>For the movies? Not really.<br /> <br /> 1) The X-Men franchise has been handled like shit and Deadpool is really the only entry so far made by people that actually get it. They've skipped over dozens of popular characters to keep going back characters from the 70s. Who's popular now has pretty much zero barring on who gets put in the films.<br /> <br /> 2) The sales of whichever character's movie just came out have a strong tendency to drop until the next movie comes out. Putting Laura up is a bad idea if she's selling well on her own.<br /> <br /> 3) The vast majority of people that go to the movies will have zero idea who the hell she is, and her backstory is extremely dense. Trying to explain her presence in the current X-Men film franchise would be an absolute nightmare for a general audience; esp. compared to, &quot;Remember how Wolverine spent time in Japan during WII? Turns out he had a kid during that.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T03:41:57-07:00","id":907049,"title":"","content":"Well, just introducing Laura in her own movie woyld be bad. But if she was introduced befire havi g to carry it herself, like say in Jackman's last outing, thst would be the best way to introduce her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:25:59-07:00","id":907133,"title":"","content":"I love Wolverine, but I think we could easily let him go for a decade. Don't recast him without a reboot. In fact straight up kill him off, it'd make a great tragedy. As far as wolverine like replacements I've seen X-23 around the internet enough they could pull her off. That said I know absolutely nothing about her. Maybe we don't need a replacement at all. Why do we need a &quot;wolverine&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:54:07-07:00","id":907187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907037#post907037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>You said the <b>Deadpool showed that lesser known characters can work on film</b>. I said <b>Deadpool is not a lesser known character</b>. You then said you were <b>talking about his supporting characters(sans Colossus).</b> lol. Clearly we're not seeing the same argument. <br /> <br /> And Guardians of the Galaxy is the only Marvel movie(counting MCU and Fox) with C-D list characters to make a billion at the box office. There are no other examples of this. None. Unless you want to count the entire Blade Trilogy. They are rolling the dice with Dr. Strange(now that there is quite a bit of faith in them), though even Strange is not a C-D lister. More B, IMO. <br /> <br /> And yes, Daken hasn't been used in over a year. He's still a CRAP character. And the writer who did most of his work with Daken, Daniel Way, no longer works for Marvel(or comics). Marvel has all but cut ties with the character. <br /> <br /> Sure, they could use him. But they won't. They will use Laura, instead. I'd wager a bet, if you'd like. And her backstory is dense? Are you familiar with Daken's? The writers will have no problem inserting a former prostitute ex-killer who was cloned from Wolverine into a movie. Zero. <br /> <br /> And the X-men movies have actually done well. First Class, Days of Future Past were both hits. Apocalypse will be a hit as well. Do they get the powers wrong? Sure. But are the movies fun? I'd say so. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And who are the dozens of &quot;popular characters&quot; Fox keeps skipping over in the films to use nothing but 70's characters?<br /> <br /> Characters like Gambit(who was created in the 90's)?<br /> <br /> Rogue(1980)<br /> <br /> Kitty Pryde(1980)<br /> <br /> Blink(90's)<br /> <br /> Emma Frost(80's)<br /> <br /> Hell, even Mystique who is arguably the star of the Fox films now, was created in the late 70's. <br /> <br /> We've seen everyone from Jubiliee, to Psylocke, to Synch in the Fox X-men films. I'd say they've done a pretty good job in recent years giving some of the lesser known characters some love. And not all of them are from the 1970's. <br /> <br /> So again, who are the dozens of popular characters they keep skipping? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T12:13:39-07:00","id":907222,"title":"","content":"So, can anyone think of any young actresses out there who would make a good Laura? Or should they gamble and cast an unknown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T13:07:08-07:00","id":907251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907049#post907049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, just introducing Laura in her own movie woyld be bad. But if she was introduced befire havi g to carry it herself, like say in Jackman's last outing, thst would be the best way to introduce her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that could be an angle looked at via the next Xmen film, with Essex corp...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907133#post907133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Wolverine, but I think we could easily let him go for a decade. Don't recast him without a reboot. In fact straight up kill him off, it'd make a great tragedy. As far as wolverine like replacements I've seen X-23 around the internet enough they could pull her off. That said I know absolutely nothing about her. Maybe we don't need a replacement at all. Why do we need a &quot;wolverine&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>With his almost immortality its gonna be hard to find a way to kill him off..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907187#post907187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've seen everyone from Jubiliee, to Psylocke, to Synch in the Fox X-men films. I'd say they've done a pretty good job in recent years giving some of the lesser known characters some love. And not all of them are from the 1970's.<br /> <br /> So again, who are the dozens of popular characters they keep skipping?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the other characters that they have yet to showcase (well imo)..<br /> Polaris/Magnetrix<br /> Cannonball (Samuel Zachary Guthrie)<br /> Thuderbird (john Proudstar)<br /> Longshot<br /> Forge (IMO one of the most iconic core Xmen)<br /> Sunspot (Roberto Da Costa)<br /> Domino<br /> Boom-boom (Tabitha smith)<br /> And since they had Psyloch, its an easy move to include her brother, Capitain Britian<br /> Several of the Guthrie family such as Husk (Paige), Icarus (Joshua),<br /> <br /> Then we get into the Xforce/Xfactor team members such as<br /> Artie maddicks, Leech Rictor, Wild child, wolfsbane, Feral..<br /> <br /> There's quite a few they have not yet touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T13:34:07-07:00","id":907263,"title":"","content":"There have been rumors of a Captain Britain TV show, but I don't know if that went anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T14:05:42-07:00","id":907278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907251#post907251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe that could be an angle looked at via the next Xmen film, with Essex corp...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With his almost immortality its gonna be hard to find a way to kill him off..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some of the other characters that they have yet to showcase (well imo)..<br /> Polaris/Magnetrix<br /> Cannonball (Samuel Zachary Guthrie)<br /> Thuderbird (john Proudstar)<br /> Longshot<br /> Forge (IMO one of the most iconic core Xmen)<br /> Sunspot (Roberto Da Costa)<br /> Domino<br /> Boom-boom (Tabitha smith)<br /> And since they had Psyloch, its an easy move to include her brother, Capitain Britian<br /> Several of the Guthrie family such as Husk (Paige), Icarus (Joshua),<br /> <br /> Then we get into the Xforce/Xfactor team members such as<br /> Artie maddicks, Leech Rictor, Wild child, wolfsbane, Feral..<br /> <br /> There's quite a few they have not yet touched.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was responding to a comment about &quot;popular&quot; characters. If Forge is considered &quot;popular,&quot; then this is a conversation I'll back out of. Paste Pot Pete, Longshot, etc. <br /> <br /> And a few of those that you listed are all but confirmed for the X-Force film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T14:24:27-07:00","id":907283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907187#post907187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly we're not seeing the same argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I was talking about films, not specific characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Guardians of the Galaxy is the only Marvel movie(counting MCU and Fox) with C-D list characters to make a billion at the box office. </div> </div> </div>Ok... Scott Lang (most people have no idea he's one of the people to be Ant-Man if they're even familiar enough with the Avengers to know about Ant-man) &quot;only&quot; brought in half a billion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are rolling the dice with Dr. Strange </div> </div> </div>No they aren't.<br /> <br /> 1) Ant-man and Guardians both worked.<br /> <br /> 2) Benedict Cumberbatch. Seriously. He's popular enough they'll make money on the film.<br /> <br /> Black Panther being announced before reactions to Civil War was rolling the dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the writer who did most of his work with Daken, Daniel Way, no longer works for Marvel(or comics). Marvel has all but cut ties with the character. </div> </div> </div>Marvel's been reducing the X-Franchise in general to reduce their presence in favor of MCU focused books and to pressure Fox to give them the movies back... they've had yet another, &quot;Wipe more mutants from the main universe,&quot; event.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And her backstory is dense? Are you familiar with Daken's? </div> </div> </div>Yes. And from a movie perspective, Daken's is easier; esp. with the existing movies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the X-men movies have actually done well. </div> </div> </div>Eh. They're a mix. Why does this point matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And who are the dozens of &quot;popular characters&quot; Fox keeps skipping over in the films to use nothing but 70's characters? </div> </div> </div>Gambit has yet to see a major role and the movie just got a major delay before production; who knows what that means.<br /> <br /> Rogue and Emma are the major exceptions.<br /> <br /> Kitty got reduced to a bit character in X3, and had one of her biggest arcs given to Logan so she can sit in a room doing almost nothing.<br /> <br /> Blink didn't even get named. She (and Warpath, Bishop, and Sunspot) were wasted as background characters that existed to be cannon fodder to Sentinels.<br /> <br /> Jubilee and Psylocke, despite being major characters in the comics, just got their first serious appearances.<br /> <br /> Synch was seen briefly in a file in X2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So again, who are the dozens of popular characters they keep skipping? </div> </div> </div>Cable and many of his associated characters via X-Force and the New Mutants, also Domino.<br /> <br /> Everyone mentioned before I could respond.<br /> <br /> Nathan Summers (though a rough one with the current stat of the books).<br /> <br /> Rachel Summers.<br /> <br /> Chamber<br /> <br /> Jamie Madrox as more than a minor lackey in one movie, along with his other unmentioned teammate in Strong Guy.<br /> <br /> Armor<br /> <br /> Darwin not dying before he can do anything.<br /> <br /> Pixie<br /> <br /> Sage<br /> <br /> Sunfire<br /> <br /> Magik.<br /> <br /> Should I keep going?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T14:27:23-07:00","id":907285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907278#post907278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a few of those that you listed are all but confirmed for the X-Force film.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one announced in 2013 and.... still hasn't happened yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:08:12-07:00","id":907356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907251#post907251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With his almost immortality its gonna be hard to find a way to kill him off..</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems they found a way to kill Apocalypse, which surprises me since Deadpool says they're going to have Cable, who, IIRC's primary nemesis is Apocalypse. That said it's been done before, though the best time might have been Days of Future past. So long as you don't go to the most ludicrious level I've heard they've gone on the comics (and they do seem to be avoiding some of that), in that he regenrated himself from like a drop of blood. Could alway have magneto rip out his skeleton and then have Phoenix ash him.<br /> <br /> Plus it would be tragic on the scales that neither Marvel nor Fox have shown they really have the fortitude to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:15:32-07:00","id":907358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907283#post907283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I keep going?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Please don't. It's clear we're not going to see eye to eye. And I'm not going to argue just for argument's sake, since subjectively you and I are on polar ends of every issue. Like, for example, what &quot;popular&quot; means. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But be happy. Cable will play a huge role in Deadpool 2!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-04-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:21:32-07:00","id":907361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907285#post907285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The one announced in 2013 and.... still hasn't happened yet?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.cinemablend.com/new/Ryan-Reynolds-Wants-Cable-Lead-Team-An-X-Force-Movie-72652.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cinemablend.com/new/Ryan-...vie-72652.html</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://therealstanlee.com/x-force-film-in-the-works/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://therealstanlee.com/main/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/logo_SMALLWHT.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://therealstanlee.com/x-force-film-in-the-works/\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found - The Real Stan Lee </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://therealstanlee.com/x-force-film-in-the-works/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://therealstanlee.com/x-force-film-in-the-works/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, the one that was fast-tracked into production thanks to the massive box office of Deadpool. They just released concept art a few months ago. It's coming.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-05-2016, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:01:40-07:00","id":907491,"title":"","content":"Those would be the same movie. X-Force has been started and stopped repeatedly once the &quot;current&quot; round of X-Men movies started up.<br /> <br /> And I'll trust it's coming when Fox announces it. Concept art, and Fox saying it's going to look at script treatments, isn't a guarantee of anything. Ryan Reynolds wanting on board (along with a few other stars) doesn't tell me it's happening any time in the near future, if at all. How long to Ryan have to beg for a Deadpool movie while Fox decided they should keep making Wolverine and Fantastic Four movies largely considered garbage?<br /> <br /> If X-Force happens, and they're smart and continue to avoid executive meddling, I'll be very happy. Trusting Fox to actually be smart with their remaining Marvel properties is something we have little reason to do (esp. if they try to convince the current main X-Men folks, and the Deadpool team, to try to become one big team instead of keeping them separate which is very likely if certain directors get their way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T08:23:30-07:00","id":907646,"title":"","content":"Now that Fox has their own guy in Simon Kinberg, in charge to handle comic to film translations after the debacle that was Fantastic Four, I'm much more optimistic about their future comic properties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:44:39-07:00","id":907845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907278#post907278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was responding to a comment about &quot;popular&quot; characters. If Forge is considered &quot;popular,&quot; then this is a conversation I'll back out of. Paste Pot Pete, Longshot, etc.<br /> <br /> And a few of those that you listed are all but confirmed for the X-Force film.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is forge not popular?? One site lists him at 27 of 50 for most popular. <br /> And that's news on the xforce film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:55:56-07:00","id":907851,"title":"","content":"Simon... co-writer and producer on the Fantastic Four debacle... Kinberg?<br /> <br /> His record is nothing to be optimistic about. The success of the films he's linked to all lean heavily on other creators.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:40:16-07:00","id":907968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=907851#post907851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simon... co-writer and producer on the Fantastic Four debacle... Kinberg?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup! He's not a terribly good writer, but as a producer and the &quot;man in charge&quot; of the Fox Marvel properties, he's got a decent track record. He produced Deadpool, too. He's been involved in a number of great movies(like The Martian, which is fantastic). <br /> <br /> I'm willing to give him the benefit of the doubt about Fantastic Four, and blame most of that on Fox trying their best(worst) to do something different. But Deadpool, and now Apocalypse(both of which he produced) were good signs to me.<br /> <br /> We'll see if it continues with his next Marvel project. I think it will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:34:22-07:00","id":908115,"title":"","content":"Ok... Just focusing on him as a producer:<br /> <br /> Fantastic Four (9% on Rotten Tomatoes)<br /> Jumper (16% on RT)<br /> Let's Be Cops (18% on RT)<br /> This Means War (26 % on RT, managed to do worse in its opening weekend than Ghost Rider 2)<br /> Chappie (31% on RT)<br /> Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter (35% on RT)<br /> X-Men: Apocalypse (48% on RT)<br /> Elysium (68% on RT)<br /> Cinderella (Live Action 2015, 83% on RT)<br /> Deadpool (83% on RT, of a good reason why RT scores aren't the be all here, but I'll get to that below)<br /> X-Men: First Class (87% on RT)<br /> X-Men: Days of Future Past (91% on RT)<br /> The Martian (92% on RT)<br /> <br /> So he's all over the place when it comes to direct adaptations. Original comedies? Both in the gutter (bad sign if he's going to have a stronger hand on any future Deadpool stuff). While not a &quot;franchise&quot; the drop from Elysium to Chappie is pretty important because that means he did nothing to help a promising director do better after District 9; and instead indulged him as things progressively got worse with each film. His job with both of those movies was to be a producer of Blomkamp, and he didn't do much of a job doing that. <br /> <br /> So RT alone isn't a bad general picture, but it isn't a complete one. Let's ignore the Apocalypse isn't getting a great critical reception. In general his involvement with the X-Franchise is generally the highlight of his career as a producer along with Cinderella and the Martian.<br /> <br /> What do all of those have in common? People that didn't need Kinberg as a strong editorial voice. Cinderella was directed by Kenneth Branagh, and The Martian was directed by Ridley Scott. These are both huge names in the industry that know exactly what they're doing. The X-Men specific films have the continual hand of Bryan Singer on them (Apocalypse the is only X-Men movie to get a poor critical response with Singer involved). Deadpool was Ryan Reynolds and Tim Miller.<br /> <br /> Simply put, this is not Fox's answer to Kevin Feige. He might be a fine producer working with people with strong visions to manage budgets and that side of things for them, but his writing credits alone show that he doesn't have the chops to be the guy managing a major film franchise and guide it to major success. What on Earth implies he's (a) the right guy for this, and (b) the guy to pin our hopes on for an X-Force movie with Cable and X-23?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:11:30-07:00","id":908132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/905932-wolverine-post-hugh-jackman?p=908115#post908115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok... What on Earth implies he's (a) the right guy for this, and (b) the guy to pin our hopes on for an X-Force movie with Cable and X-23?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that there is not a single creative voice as a director or producer that has a perfect track record(like Ridley Scott or Kenneth Branaugh, who've both made their fair share of stinkers), <b>I've enjoyed every X-Film he's been a part of</b>. Counting Deadpool, he's 4 for 5 with Marvel movies with me.<br /> <br /> I loved First Class. I enjoyed Days of Future Past. I loved Deadpool. I enjoyed Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> To me, as long as Fox has the X-men rights(unfortunately), he's the best man for the job.<br /> <br /> It's clear you disagree. That's cool, too.<br /> <br /> Have a good night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 06-06-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}